<BaseLayout
    title="About | Bimal Kaur"
    description="About Bimal Kaur — reflections on cybersecurity, technology risk, leadership and human behaviour."
>

<article class="about">

    <h1>About</h1>

    <p>
        I work at the intersection of cybersecurity, technology and human behaviour - where the interesting problems usually begin.
    </p>

    <p>
        Years in cyber advisory have taught me that failures rarely come from technology alone. They emerge from decisions, assumptions and the small things people overlook.
    </p>

    <p>
        My work spans cybersecurity advisory, risk management, detection engineering and complex technology
        environments - helping organisations understand their exposure, strengthen
        resilience and make better decisions in an increasingly connected world.
    </p>

    <p>
        Because technology can be engineered. Good judgement is harder to configure. Less about chasing every new trend. More about understanding what lasts.
    </p>

</article>


